{
  "requirement": "The SDK offers this `Sources` method and exposes the `search_structure`\ncommand through its source tools.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Sources {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Search source structure.\n    pub async fn search_structure(\n        &self,\n        query: &StructuralQuery,\n    ) -> Result<StructuralMatches, SourceError>;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Structural obligations**\n1. `Sources` offers `pub async fn search_structure(&self, query: &StructuralQuery) -> Result<StructuralMatches, SourceError>`.\n2. The SDK exposes a `search_structure` command through its source tools.\n\n**Obligation 1: the method**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/public.rs#impl[Sources]/fn[search_structure]` has exactly the required signature: `&self`, `query: &StructuralQuery`, and `Result<StructuralMatches, SourceError>`. It is `pub async` and carries the `{impl}` reference.\n- It delegates to `self.analysis.search_structure(query)`. The `Sources` struct holds `analysis: SourceAnalysis<LocalSources>`.\n- `LocalSources` implements `SourceProvider` with `type Error = SourceError`, as the search for `type Error` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs` shows. So `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources.rs#impl[SourceAnalysis<P>]/fn[search_structure]`, which returns `Result<StructuralMatches, P::Error>`, yields `SourceError` for `Sources`.\n- That function forwards to `self.provider.search_structure(query, &self.languages)`, so the method delegates through the provider interface.\n\n**Obligation 2: the tool**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/sources.rs#impl[SourceSession<...>/ToolSession<D>]/fn[definitions]` declares a `search_structure` tool. Its parameters are `language` and `rule` (both required), plus `prefix` and `limit`.\n- `fn[dispatch]` in the same impl handles `\"search_structure\"`. It reads `language`, `rule` and the scope, builds a `StructuralQuery`, and calls `self.tools.analysis.search_structure(...)`. `fn[dispatch]` carries `{impl}` references to the `.behavior` and `.inputs` requirements. That is consistent with this requirement's `.fn` reference sitting on `fn[definitions]`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs` has a separate fixed project tool set. Its `Session` `fn[definitions]` and `fn[dispatch]` also expose `search_structure` and call `Sources::search_structure`. That is a different tool surface. Its `read_source` takes `path`, not `resource`, and is likewise not marked for any `.fn` requirement. It only calls the already-marked method, so I treat it as a caller and not as a required root.\n\n**Result**\nBoth structural obligations are met. There are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments, and I found no structural gap. The requirement imposes no behavioral obligation beyond the method and tool existing.",
